{"name":"Only Oatmeal","hex":"#d4cdb5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"only","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alone in a category.","Singularly superior; the best."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Without others or anything further; exclusively.","No more than; just."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/only"},{"term":"oatmeal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Meal made from rolled or round oats.","A breakfast cereal made from rolled oats, cooked in milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light greyish brown colour, like that of oatmeal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oatmeal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oatmeal","blocks":[{"text":"Oatmeal is a preparation of oats that have been dehusked, steamed, and flattened, or a coarse flour of hulled oat grains (groats) that have either been milled (ground), rolled, or steel-cut. Ground oats are also called white oats. Steel-cut oats are known as coarse oatmeal, Irish oatmeal, or pinhead oats. Rolled oats were traditionally thick old-fashioned oats, but they can be made thinner or smaller and may be categorized as quick oatmeal or instant oatmeal depending on the cooking time required, which is determined by the size of the oats and the amount of precooking."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Oatmeal.jpg/330px-Oatmeal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oatmeal","wikidata":"Q26883501"},{"title":"List of Crayola crayon colors","blocks":[{"text":"Since the introduction of Crayola drawing crayons by Binney & Smith in 1903, more than 200 colors have been produced in a wide variety of assortments. The table below represents all of the colors found in regular Crayola assortments from 1903 to the present. Since the introduction of fluorescent crayons in the 1970s, the standard colors have been complemented by a number of specialty crayon assortments, represented in subsequent tables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Crayola1.jpg/330px-Crayola1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Crayola_crayon_colors","wikidata":"Q6568034"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/091223_galletas_de_avena.JPG/500px-091223_galletas_de_avena.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/091223_galletas_de_avena.JPG/500px-091223_galletas_de_avena.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Oatmeal cookies made with oatmeal, flour, sugar and butter","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A091223_galletas_de_avena.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cooked_oat_groats.jpg/250px-Cooked_oat_groats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cooked_oat_groats.jpg/500px-Cooked_oat_groats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cooked_oat_groats.jpg/250px-Cooked_oat_groats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACooked_oat_groats.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Cooked_steel-cut_oats.jpg/250px-Cooked_steel-cut_oats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Cooked_steel-cut_oats.jpg/500px-Cooked_steel-cut_oats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Cooked_steel-cut_oats.jpg/25